        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Alesia</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">September 52 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Around the Gallic oppidum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alesia-city">Alesia</a>, a centre of the Mandubii, most probably on Mont <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auxois">Auxois</a> above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alise-sainte-reine">Alise-Sainte-Reine</a> in the Côte-d'Or, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> under the proconsul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>, against a confederation of Gallic tribes under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arverni">Arverni</a>; about 80,000 men are said to have been in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alesia-city">Alesia</a>, and the relief force is put at a quarter of a million by Caesar and at 50,000 to 100,000 by modern historians</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The relief force was beaten off and fled, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a> surrendered, and the Gallic revolt collapsed</span></div>
        </div>
